  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉⲡⲉⲓⲇⲏ ⲁⲡⲁⲡⲟⲥⲧⲟⲗⲟⲥ ϫⲟⲟⲥ · ϫⲉⲟⲩϩⲉⲗⲡⲓⲍ ⲉⲩⲛⲁⲩ ⲉⲣⲟⲥ ⲛⲟⲩϩⲉⲗⲡⲓⲍ ⲁⲛ ⲧⲉ ⲉⲧⲉⲧⲁⲓ ⲧⲉ ⲧⲙⲛⲧⲣⲙⲙⲁⲟ ⲙⲡⲉⲓⲕⲟⲥⲙⲟⲥ ⲉⲧⲛⲁⲡⲁⲣⲁⲅⲉ ⲛⲧϩⲉ ⲛⲟⲩ**ϩⲁⲗⲟⲩⲥ** ·",
      "english": "for the Apostle saith, 'The hope which is seen is not hope,' that is to say, the riches of this world which shall pass away like the snow (or, frost).",
      "source": "Encomium on Victor part 3",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pscelestinus.encomium.budge:56-103",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲱ ϩⲁⲡⲁⲝ ϩⲁⲡⲗⲱⲥ ϩⲱⲃ ⲛⲓⲙ ⲉⲧⲙⲡⲉⲓⲙⲁ ⲉⲩⲟ ⲛⲧϩⲉ ⲛⲉⲓ**ϩⲁⲗⲟⲩⲥ** ⲙⲛϩⲉⲛⲣⲁⲥⲟⲩ ·",
      "english": "And in short, everything which is in this world becometh like unto the web of the spider, and like unto dreams.",
      "source": "On Penitence and Abstinence, part 2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:johnconst.penitence.budge:120-241",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲙⲛⲛⲥⲱⲥ ⲟⲩⲛⲟⲩⲃ ⲏ ⲟⲩϩⲁⲧ ⲛⲁⲓ ⲧⲏⲣⲟⲩ ϩⲉⲛ**ϩⲁⲗⲟⲩⲥ** ⲛⲉ ·",
      "english": "or to gold or silver, for all these things afterwards become fetters to thee;",
